WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.240
Look at a tree trunk or a rock in a Virginia park.

2
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.360
Some gray-green crusty patches there are lichens.

3
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.120
Each lichen looks like one living thing.

4
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:16.920
But it is a partnership of very different living things, growing as one body.

5
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:21.760
Do living things that live close together help each other, or hurt each other?

6
00:00:22.733 --> 00:00:27.633
Symbiosis is a close relationship between individuals of different species living

7
00:00:27.633 --> 00:00:32.253
together. The partners stay in close contact, often for a long time.

8
00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:37.373
A bird that eats one seed and flies off is not in a symbiosis with the plant.

9
00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:41.937
A lichen is a fungus and an alga living as one body.

10
00:00:42.797 --> 00:00:44.857
An alga is a tiny green living thing.

11
00:00:45.597 --> 00:00:46.997
The fungus forms the outside.

12
00:00:47.877 --> 00:00:50.357
It shelters its partner and helps keep it moist.

13
00:00:51.257 --> 00:00:53.117
The alga makes sugar by photosynthesis.

14
00:00:54.057 --> 00:00:55.537
That food feeds both partners.

15
00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:00.270
Scientists sort symbiosis by what each partner gains or loses.

16
00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:05.950
In mutualism, all the partners benefit, like the fungus and alga in a lichen.

17
00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:10.530
In commensalism, one partner benefits and the others are unaffected.

18
00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:15.490
A lichen on tree bark gets a place to live, and the tree seems unaffected.

19
00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.810
In parasitism, one partner benefits and the others are harmed.

20
00:01:20.783 --> 00:01:24.283
A blacklegged tick can drink blood from a deer for several days.

21
00:01:25.203 --> 00:01:26.323
The tick is the parasite.

22
00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:30.663
The deer is its host, the living thing a parasite lives on or in.

23
00:01:31.403 --> 00:01:36.183
A parasite usually feeds over days or longer, and usually does not kill its host.

24
00:01:37.043 --> 00:01:39.103
A predator kills and eats its prey quickly.

25
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:43.517
So, do living things that live close together help each other?

26
00:01:44.397 --> 00:01:46.037
Sometimes both partners benefit.

27
00:01:46.897 --> 00:01:49.457
Sometimes one benefits and the other is unaffected.

28
00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:51.557
Sometimes one is harmed.

29
00:01:52.817 --> 00:01:54.077
Partners do not choose to be kind.

30
00:01:55.037 --> 00:01:59.297
A symbiosis carries on because living this way let the partners, or at least the

31
00:01:59.297 --> 00:02:01.357
parasite, survive and reproduce.
